":"2020"},{"detail":"The Democratic Party of Oregon used STAR Voting for their elections for delegates to the 2020 Democratic convention.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"Democratic Party of Oregon","scope":"party","source":"wikipedia","state":"OR","status":"in use","system":"STAR","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STAR_voting","year":"2020"},{"detail":"A ballot initiative for the city of Eugene was attempted but no measure was held in 2020 after the City Council deadlocked and the Mayor voted against referral.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"OR","status":"proposed","system":"STAR","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STAR_voting","year":"2020"},{"detail":"A measure in Oakridge, Oregon to implement STAR voting for three elections failed with 46% approval.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"OR","status":"rejected","system":"STAR","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STAR_voting","year":"2024"},{"detail":"South Carolina allows absentee voters to submit ranked ballots in runoff elections so their votes can count in the second round if their first choice is eliminated.","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","party":"","scope":"statewide","source":"wikipedia","state":"SC","status":"in use","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant-runoff_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Approval voting is used in internal elections by the Green Party of Texas.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"Green Party of Texas","scope":"party","source":"wikipedia","state":"TX","status":"in use","system":"Approval","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Approval voting is used in internal elections by the Libertarian Party of Texas.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"Libertarian Party of Texas","scope":"party","source":"wikipedia","state":"TX","status":"in use","system":"Approval","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Approval voting is used in internal elections by the Libertarian National Committee.","model":"qwen/qwen3.8-27b","party":"Libertarian National Committee","scope":"party","source":"wikipedia","state":"US","status":"in use","system":"Approval","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","year":""},{"detail":"Utah passed a law allowing municipalities to opt into a temporary instant-runoff voting trial pilot project running through the 2025 elections.","model":"gemini-3.8-flash","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"UT","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2018"},{"detail":"The Virginia legislature passed a bill providing municipalities with a local option to use single transferable vote through 2031.","model":"gemini-3.8-flash","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"VA","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"2020"},{"detail":"Seattle voters chose ranked-choice voting over approval voting after first voting in favor of changing the city's election system.","model":"gemini-3.8-flash","party":"","scope":"local","source":"wikipedia","state":"WA","status":"adopted","system":"RCV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","year":"unknown"}],"partial":true,"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranked-choice_voting_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approval_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STAR_voting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_reform_in_the_United_States","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inst